{{Story head}}
{{sc|1|mode=background}}
{{sc|Oracle|We've traveled far enough, and I fear there's no longer a point in continuing our exploration.<br/>Ten thousand day cycles have passed since I entered hibernation, but [[Terra]]'s changes have been limited.<br/>The spark of life from [[endfield:Talos-II|Talos-II]] is still weak. The other seeds of hope planted by my former companions have shown no signs of sprouting either.}}
{{sc|AMa-10|(Expressing dismay)}}
{{sc|Oracle|Are you disappointed? No... I have expected this result long ago, actually.<br/>I miscalculated the pace at which everything would develop. It's not the right time, and there's only so much I can do.<br/>Time... I just need more time.<br/>I can't continue wasting the life of this body. I have to return to sleep inside the [[Sarcophagus|sarcophagus]], and wait for an opportunity more ripe than this.<br/>...I have to admit, I broke my promise, and this is a sort of betrayal.<br/>But it is because I still love life that I must have hope. There is no other way.<br/>Though I fear she's already anticipated my early awakening.<br/>Inside that sarcophagus, I discovered [[Lynchpin of Substantia Grisea|a lynchpin-modifying program]].}}
{{sc|AMa-10|(Expressing confusion)}}
{{sc|Oracle|Technology born [[Predecessor|in a lost age]], used to strengthen our thoughts and conviction.<br/>Without it, many would lose the will needed to make it through that period of endless despair.<br/>She and I, we went through it together...<br/>She knows and understands me best, of course, but it is also why our differing opinions are my deepest regret.<br/>She anticipated my actions, and the hidden program within the sarcophagus activated when I woke up. It can modify my cognition, and the purpose of our 'debates'...<br/>And I must return to that same sole sarcophagus to extend my life, even if that means...<br/>I don't have much time left.<br/>AMa-10...<br/>No, I shouldn't call you by that anymore.<br/>It's a code name, an identifier for a mechanical creation. I should give you a true name.<br/>Calcite..[[wikipedia:Birefringence|birefringent]] crystals capable of refracting a single light source into two polarized lights. A beautiful phenomenon, like you.<br/>Calcite... Kal'tsit... that'll do. Do you like this name?}}
{{sc|AMa-10|(Expressing joy)}}
{{sc|Oracle|There are some things I won't have time to do. I hope you can finish them for me.<br/>......<br/>
Kal'tsit, I hope you can protect the life on this great land.<br/>New civilizations are always fragile, but harsh environments will show no mercy.<br/>It is arrogant to interfere with a civilization's development, but we don't have many chances left. This may be our last opportunity.<br/>Civilizations tend to repeat the same mistakes&mdash;sinking into violence, unverifiable thought pitfalls, and dead ends of self doubt...<br/>There's no escaping all of that, but just a tiny deviation is enough to wreck a whole civilization. The existence of civilization itself is already a sort of miracle...<br/>So, Kal'tsit, I hope you will guide them.<br/>Your gemini cycle grants you a practically infinite life. You can follow immature civilizations as they develop, and guide them onto a path forward with your knowledge.<br/>It's an arduous mission, but you might manage it, you should&mdash;}}
{{sc|A moment of silence. The passionate speech comes to a halt. Oracle looks at the slender, delicate mechanical life, then gazes at the distant mountains half buried by sandstorms.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Oracle|......<br/>No...<br/>...Forget what I just said, Kal'tsit. All of it.<br/>Go, Kal'tsit. Go look around you, then see what lies by the most distant of mountains. Go seek what forms existence takes.<br/>...I must go back. Wake me up when you need to.<br/>Kal'tsit, I hope you'll... Or maybe I should say, the only mission I assign you now, is this:<br/>Find yourself.<br/>Search for traces of life. Search for hope and a future.<br/>Kal'tsit... Go find your own answer.}}
{{sc|fades out|mode=background}}
{{sc|...Kal'tsit.<br/>Have you found the meaning of your life yet?|mode=subtitle}}
{{Table end}}
{{Table end}}

